      "heading": "B — Audience",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience, Section Five Impaired driving\n\nThe audience is first-time, never-licensed applicants preparing for the West Virginia Class E knowledge examination, reading at a plain-English level with no prior driving knowledge assumed. Section Five teaches why impairment is dangerous, where the legal thresholds sit, what each DUI tier costs, and how drowsiness impairs like alcohol. It depends on the definitions chapter for blood alcohol concentration, driving under the influence and implied consent. The rules progress from the effects of alcohol and the thresholds, through implied consent and the penalty tiers, to the Interlock Program and drowsy driving.\n",
